ta","data":[{"unit":1,"title":3,"area":83,"prev":85,"next":87,"titles":90,"firmware":259},{"id":2,"title":3,"aliases":4,"area":11,"order":12,"path":13,"context":14,"summary":19,"status":20,"firmware":21,"facts":26,"procedures":43,"parameters":44,"related":69,"body":72,"sources":73,"official_url":30,"controls":78},"fx.lofi","Lofi effect",[5,6,7,8,9,10],"lofi","lo-fi","bitcrusher","bit crusher","sample rate reduction","decimator","fx",40,"knowledge/manual/units/fx/lofi.md",{"modes":15,"screens":17},[16],"auxiliary",[18],"M1","A bitcrusher for FX I or FX II; `M1` sets the sample rate, bit depth, a quality control and drift, which spreads the result in stereo.","current",{"min":22,"changed_in":23,"guide_version":24,"verified_on":25},"1.0.9",[],"1.1.15",null,[27,32,35,40],{"id":28,"text":29,"source":30,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":31},"what","Lofi is a bitcrusher. It roughens a sound by lowering its sample rate and bit depth, for lo-fi styles or just extra grit.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/fx#lofi","official",{"id":33,"text":34,"source":30,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":31},"quality","The guide gives no detail about the quality control (`E3`) beyond its name.",{"id":36,"text":37,"source":38,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":39},"start-values","A lofi page opens on rate 50, bits 73, quality 61 and drift 99 (one video, OS 1.0, the first seconds of the page).","docs/research/78-overnight-accuracy.md#log","community",{"id":41,"text":42,"source":38,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":39},"rate-keeps-treble","Lofi at a low rate still keeps some treble, with music staying up to about 3 to 5 kHz at rate 16, about 5.5 kHz at 44 and about 8 kHz at 68 (one video, OS 1.0, a single sighting).",[],[45,53,59,63],{"screen":18,"encoder":46,"layer":47,"keys":48,"name":49,"range":25,"default":25,"cc":50,"cc_confidence":51,"note":52,"source":30,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":31},"E1","base","turn E1","rate",12,"community-verified","sample rate of the effect",{"screen":18,"encoder":54,"layer":47,"keys":55,"name":56,"range":25,"default":25,"cc":57,"cc_confidence":51,"note":58,"source":30,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":31},"E2","turn E2","bits",13,"bit depth (the guide says bitrate)",{"screen":18,"encoder":60,"layer":47,"keys":61,"name":33,"range":25,"default":25,"cc":62,"cc_confidence":51,"note":25,"source":30,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":31},"E3","turn E3",14,{"screen":18,"encoder":64,"layer":47,"keys":65,"name":66,"range":25,"default":25,"cc":67,"cc_confidence":51,"note":68,"source":30,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":31},"E4","turn E4","drift",15,"stereo spread of the output",[70,71],"fx.overview","fx.distortion","Lofi degrades audio the digital way: fewer samples per second and fewer bits per sample. Small\namounts add a dusty edge to drums and keys; extreme settings turn anything into crunchy, aliased\nnoise. Drift widens the crushed signal across the stereo field. Sent from a few tracks at once, it\ngives a whole mix a shared worn-out character.",[74,76],{"url":30,"kind":75},"guide",{"url":38,"kind":77},"research",[79,80,81,82],"encoder.1","encoder.2","encoder.3","encoder.4",{"id":11,"title":84},"Effects",{"id":71,"title":86},"Distortion effect",{"id":88,"title":89},"fx.phaser","Phaser effect",{"basics.key-notation":91,"basics.main-modes":92,"basics.modules":93,"basics.track-buttons":94,"basics.linked-tracks":95,"basics.patterns-scenes-songs":96,"basics.workflow":97,"basics.firmware-versions":98,"hardware.layout":99,"hardware.power-and-charging":100,"hardware.connectors":101,"hardware.specifications":102,"hardware.te-boot":103,"hardware.firmware-update":104,"hardware.factory-reset":105,"hardware.system-menu":106,"hardware.safety-and-care":107,"hardware.in-the-box":108,"sequencer.overview":109,"sequencer.step-entry":110,"sequencer.step-recording":111,"sequencer.live-recording":112,"sequencer.extend-notes":